# Trim the upload, never the build inputs.
#
# AKBAR-NAWASUNDA-ASSETS/ and scripts/ deliberately stay IN the upload:
#   - src/assets/manifest.ts statically imports the original artwork from
#     AKBAR-NAWASUNDA-ASSETS/ at build time. Removing it produces
#     "Module not found" on Vercel while local builds stay green.
#   - scripts/ holds the build/QA helpers the Vercel project commands may call.
# `outputFileTracingExcludes` in next.config.ts is what keeps these out of the
# deployed function bundle; .vercelignore only controls what gets uploaded.
# Run `npm run vercel:audit` (also a CI step) before editing this file.

docs/
*.md
!README.md
artifacts/
review-shots/
tests/
coverage/
*.test.ts
*.test.tsx
*.spec.ts
*.spec.tsx
.next/cache/
